From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 20:41:25 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Compare the prefix range span to the bit count as unsigned

PrefixRangeBitmap<U>::Initialize() shifts the span until it fits the
bitmap, comparing (span >> shift) with max_bits, an idx_t, which for
an instantiation with a signed U is a comparison across signedness
under -Wsign-compare. The span is never negative, and the line below
already converts the same expression with UnsafeNumericCast<idx_t>, so
the loop condition does the same.

Carried here until upstream takes it; not proposed upstream yet.

---
 src/duckdb/src/planner/filter/table_filter_prefix_range_function.cpp | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/duckdb/src/planner/filter/table_filter_prefix_range_function.cpp b/src/duckdb/src/planner/filter/table_filter_prefix_range_function.cpp
index 62bfabad83..2544a30cf7 100644
--- a/src/duckdb/src/planner/filter/table_filter_prefix_range_function.cpp
+++ b/src/duckdb/src/planner/filter/table_filter_prefix_range_function.cpp
@@ -65,7 +65,7 @@ public:
 		span = span_p;
 		shift = 0;
 
-		while ((span >> shift) >= max_bits) {
+		while (UnsafeNumericCast<idx_t>(span >> shift) >= max_bits) {
 			shift++;
 		}
 
